---
import Base       from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Nav        from "../components/Nav.astro";
import PageHero   from "../components/PageHero.astro";
import Footer     from "../components/Footer.astro";

const title = "Terms of Service — MeshWG";
const description = "The terms you accept when you use MeshWG. Written to be readable, not to hide things.";

const effective = "2026-05-13";
---

<Base title={title} description={description}>
  <Nav />
  <PageHero
    eyebrow="/ terms"
    title="The terms you accept when you use MeshWG."
    lede={`Effective ${effective}. By signing up or using meshwg.com, you agree to these terms. We've tried to make them readable.`}
  />

  <section class="legal">
    <div class="wrap">

      <article>
        <h2>1. What MeshWG is</h2>
        <p>
          MeshWG is a hosted mesh VPN + zero-trust access controller built on
          WireGuard. We run a multi-tenant controller at vpn.meshwg.com; you connect
          your routers, laptops, and servers to it; tunnels between your devices
          establish through us and stay running on your devices.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>2. Account</h2>
        <p>
          You're responsible for your account and its credentials. You confirm that
          the email address you signed up with is one you control. You agree not to
          share account credentials with people who shouldn't have them; if you need
          to add team members, use the per-user features in the dashboard.
        </p>
        <p>
          You must be 16 or older to use MeshWG. We don't knowingly serve anyone younger.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>3. Acceptable use</h2>
        <p>
          MeshWG is for legitimate networking. You agree not to use it to:
        </p>
        <ul class="bullets">
          <li>Send spam, run phishing infrastructure, or distribute malware.</li>
          <li>Conduct DDoS attacks, port-scan third parties, or any other network abuse.</li>
          <li>Host or distribute content that's illegal where you live or where our infrastructure runs.</li>
          <li>Circumvent the rate limits, machine quotas, or other technical controls in the product.</li>
          <li>Reverse-engineer, decompile, or otherwise attempt to derive the source of the controller. The product is closed source.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>
          We may suspend or terminate accounts engaged in any of the above, without notice if the abuse is ongoing.
          We try to email first when we can.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>4. What you own</h2>
        <p>
          You own your machines, your private keys (we never see them), and your
          configurations. You retain all rights to the data inside your tunnels. We
          claim no ownership over anything you put into the product.
        </p>
        <p>
          We own MeshWG itself: the controller code, dashboard UI, brand, and
          documentation. Using the product doesn't transfer any of that to you.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>5. Pricing and payment</h2>
        <p>
          The Free tier covers up to 2 machines, indefinitely. No credit card required.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Cloud tier is $1 per machine per month billed annually, or $3 per
          machine per month billed monthly. The first 2 machines in any paid account
          remain free; you only pay for the third and beyond. Billing is handled by
          Stripe.
        </p>
        <p>
          The Pro tier is custom pricing for larger deployments, dedicated
          infrastructure, or custom needs — contact us.
        </p>
        <p>
          We reserve the right to change pricing with 30 days' notice. Existing annual
          subscriptions are honored at their original price for the remainder of the
          term.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>6. Cancellation and refunds</h2>
        <p>
          You can cancel any paid plan from your dashboard at any time. Monthly plans
          stop billing at the next cycle. Annual plans continue serving you at the paid
          tier through the end of the year you've paid for; after the year, machines
          above the free 2 go read-only until you re-subscribe or remove them. No
          partial refunds on annual.
        </p>
        <p>
          If you've been charged in error or you genuinely never used the service,
          email <a href="mailto:hello@meshwg.com">hello@meshwg.com</a> within 30 days
          and we'll make it right.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>7. Service availability</h2>
        <p>
          MeshWG is provided <strong>as-is</strong>. We don't promise specific uptime
          on the Free or Cloud tiers. Pro contracts can include an SLA on request.
        </p>
        <p>
          A nice architectural property worth knowing: when MeshWG itself goes
          offline, the tunnels between your already-onboarded peers <strong>keep
          working</strong>, because WireGuard runs on your devices, not on our servers.
          You can't add new peers or change rules during an outage, but existing
          connectivity is unaffected.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>8. Disclaimer of warranties</h2>
        <p>
          MeshWG is provided without warranties of any kind, express or implied,
          including merchantability, fitness for a particular purpose, and
          non-infringement. We don't guarantee that the service will be uninterrupted,
          error-free, or that defects will be corrected immediately.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>9. Limitation of liability</h2>
        <p>
          To the maximum extent permitted by law: MeshWG (and its operators, employees,
          and contractors) are not liable for indirect, incidental, special,
          consequential, or punitive damages, including loss of profits, data,
          goodwill, or other intangible losses. Our total aggregate liability for any
          claim arising out of these terms or the service is limited to the amount you
          paid us in the 12 months preceding the claim, or $50, whichever is greater.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>10. Indemnity</h2>
        <p>
          If we're sued because of what <em>you</em> did with the service — illegal
          use, infringement of someone else's rights, abuse of third parties — you
          agree to defend us and cover the costs.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>11. Changes to these terms</h2>
        <p>
          We may update these terms. Material changes get emailed to the address on
          file with at least 30 days' notice before they take effect. Continuing to use
          the service after the effective date constitutes acceptance.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>12. Governing law</h2>
        <p>
          These terms are governed by the laws of India, without regard to conflict-of-law
          principles. Any disputes will be resolved in the courts of Mumbai, Maharashtra,
          unless mandatory consumer-protection law in your jurisdiction says otherwise.
        </p>
      </article>

      <article>
        <h2>13. Contact</h2>
        <p>
          Questions: <a href="mailto:hello@meshwg.com">hello@meshwg.com</a><br>
          Security: <a href="mailto:security@meshwg.com">security@meshwg.com</a>
        </p>
      </article>

    </div>
  </section>

  <Footer />
</Base>

<style>
  .legal { padding: 64px 0 128px; }
  .legal article { margin-bottom: 48px; max-width: 720px; }
  .legal article:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .legal h2 {
    font-size: 20px; font-weight: 500;
    letter-spacing: -.012em;
    margin: 0 0 16px;
  }
  .legal p {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.7;
    margin: 0 0 14px;
  }
  .legal p:last-child { margin-bottom: 0; }
  .legal strong { color: var(--text); font-weight: 500; }
  .legal em { color: var(--text); font-style: italic; }
  .legal a { color: var(--accent); }
  .legal a:hover { color: var(--accent-strong); }
  .bullets {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0; margin: 0 0 14px;
    display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px;
  }
  .bullets li {
    color: var(--text-2);
    font-size: 15px; line-height: 1.65;
    padding-left: 22px;
    position: relative;
  }
  .bullets li::before {
    content: "—";
    position: absolute; left: 0; top: 0;
    color: var(--text-4);
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
  }

  @media (max-width: 980px) {
    .legal { padding: 32px 0 64px; }
    .legal article { margin-bottom: 36px; }
  }
</style>
